# Pinned aggregate sha256 of the ZisK 1.3.1-alpha proving keys that Rome's proofs are made with: provingKey (about 15.8 GB
# unpacked, 5.1 GB compressed) and provingKeySnark (about 26.2 GB unpacked, 21.9 GB compressed). check-keys.sh checks them
# against this file before every prover start; see its header for the format and the hash recipe. File names are sorted
# bytewise (LC_ALL=C), so a pin does not depend on the locale of the host that checks it.
#
# The *.consttree, *.consttree_gpu and *.const_gpu files are not hashed. The host's setup generates them from the keys (a
# GPU install writes a *.const_gpu file per circuit and the PLONK step's recursivef.consttree, recursivef.const_gpu and recursivef.consttree_gpu), so they are left out of the hash;
# each proof's local verify still uses them.
#
# These are the keys that `ziskup -v 1.3.1-alpha --provingkey` and `ziskup setup_snark` install (see docs/PROVER-HOST.md).
# A different ZisK release has different keys: do not re-pin to make a mismatch go away, install the release this file was
# made for. Pin a key set of your own, on purpose, with:
#   ZISK_HOME=<where the keys are> MANIFEST=./prover/keys.sha256 bash ./prover/check-keys.sh --write
46602f3d41139d8e8f0f73bf59c17310061b47a74e75c919495de6d0897c343d  provingKey
ebbc9dd8928c9ac0779721f0404ccb577fe1c7604dba5259a207bdc265f2de54  provingKeySnark
